ITEM 78 -- a_0 as a Hubble-tension meter
====================================================================================================================
  canonical: a_0 = (c/2) sqrt(G rho_Lambda), rho_Lambda from the CMB -- a_0 does not know about the local H_0 at all
  alt footing with H_0 = 67.4: rho_total = 8.533e-27 kg/m^3 -> a_0 = 1.1312e-10 m/s^2
  alt footing with H_0 = 73.0: rho_total = 1.001e-26 kg/m^3 -> a_0 = 1.2252e-10 m/s^2
  so on the alt footing the two H_0 values give a_0 values 0.0347 dex apart (8.3%), while on the canonical footing they give the SAME a_0
  [PASS] 78 the idea works in principle and fails in practice at today's precision: the two H_0 values differ by only 0.07 dex in a_0 on the alt footing, well inside the 15% (0.06 dex) with which a_0 is currently measured -- so a_0 is not yet a Hubble-tension meter, and would need the ~3% measurement item 64 could not reach   (H_0 lever = 0.0347 dex vs a current a_0 precision of 14.8% = 0.060 dex; a 3% measurement would separate them at 2.7 sigma)

